'' EndOfStatement skips forward to the next EOL. A single-line IF's inner statement
'' has ALREADY consumed the line's EOL, so running it again for the IF skipped to the
'' NEXT one and swallowed everything between -- an 'end sub', a 'wend' -- whole. It
'' only surfaced when the IF was the LAST statement of a block; anywhere else the
'' token it ate was an ordinary statement that reparsed without complaint.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ast tests/parser/src/singleline-if.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0405
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0408
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 0
